From 43f6429106d776c4789084b2ff7ca65b559bff76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: guillermo dieguez <dev@guillermodieguez.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:08:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: reuse the last iOS screenshot when nothing touched the
 screen

A screen static check that follows a view hierarchy read, such as the one an assertion makes before the next tap, takes two screenshots even though the previous check captured the screen a few hundred milliseconds before and nothing has touched it since. Each screenshot costs about 60 ms on a simulator.

The driver now tells the runner whether a command that can change the screen ran since its last check: a tap, a swipe, typing, a key, an app launch or stop, a link, or a permission change. When nothing did, the runner compares the new screenshot against its last one if that one is less than a second old. Any of those commands still makes the next check take two.
